[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/milvus-io/milvus/issues/comments/4473639581","html_url":"https://github.com/milvus-io/milvus/issues/49843#issuecomment-4473639581","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/milvus-io/milvus/issues/49843","id":4473639581,"node_id":"IC_kwDODHDyxM8AAAABCqZSnQ","user":{"login":"yanliang567","id":82361606,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgyMzYxNjA2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/82361606?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanliang567","html_url":"https://github.com/yanliang567","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanliang567/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanliang567/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanliang567/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanliang567/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanliang567/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanliang567/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanliang567/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanliang567/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yanliang567/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-18T02:08:40Z","updated_at":"2026-05-18T02:08:40Z","body":"/assign @MrPresent-Han \n/unassign","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/milvus-io/milvus/issues/comments/4473639581/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/milvus-io/milvus/issues/comments/4574915821","html_url":"https://github.com/milvus-io/milvus/issues/49843#issuecomment-4574915821","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/milvus-io/milvus/issues/49843","id":4574915821,"node_id":"IC_kwDODHDyxM8AAAABEK-s7Q","user":{"login":"<submitter>","id":212866814,"node_id":"U_kgDODLAW_g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/212866814?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/<submitter>","html_url":"https://github.com/<submitter>","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/<submitter>/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/<submitter>/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/<submitter>/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/<submitter>/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/<submitter>/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/<submitter>/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/<submitter>/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/<submitter>/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/<submitter>/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-29T12:21:47Z","updated_at":"2026-05-29T12:21:47Z","body":"## Independent Verification — Confirmed on v2.6.16\n\nI independently verified this bug using automated parameter validation testing (TestVDB deterministic generator). Here are the additional findings:\n\n### Key Evidence: `alter_properties` correctly rejects while `create` silently drops\n\nThis inconsistency makes the bug particularly dangerous — users receive a success response and **assume TTL was set**, when it was actually silently discarded.\n\n```\n# create with ttl=-100 → SUCCESS (but TTL is NOT set)\nPOST /v2/vectordb/collections/create\n{\"collectionName\":\"test\",\"dimension\":4,\"metricType\":\"L2\",\"properties\":{\"collection.ttl.seconds\":-100}}\n→ {\"code\":0,\"data\":{}}\n\n# describe → NO TTL property\nPOST /v2/vectordb/collections/describe\n{\"collectionName\":\"test\"}\n→ \"properties\": [{\"key\": \"timezone\", \"value\": \"UTC\"}]   ← TTL missing!\n\n# alter_properties with ttl=-100 → CORRECTLY REJECTED\nPOST /v2/vectordb/collections/alter_properties\n{\"collectionName\":\"test\",\"properties\":{\"collection.ttl.seconds\":-100}}\n→ {\"code\":1100,\"message\":\"collection TTL is out of range, expect [-1, 3155760000], got -100: invalid parameter\"}\n```\n\n### Additional edge case: `collection.ttl.seconds=-1`\n\nThe valid range is `[-1, 3155760000]` where `-1` means \"TTL disabled\". However, `create` also silently drops `ttl.seconds=-1` — the collection is created without any TTL property, which happens to be the same as \"TTL disabled\" (the default). This is technically correct behavior but inconsistent with the documented range, and the silent drop makes it impossible for users to distinguish between \"I set TTL=-1\" and \"I forgot to set TTL\".\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nThis is a **data safety issue**: if a user creates a collection with `collection.ttl.seconds=3600` (1 hour TTL) but accidentally types `-3600`, the API returns success and the collection retains data indefinitely with no TTL. The user has no way to know the TTL was not set without explicitly calling `describe`.\n\n### Suggested Fix\n\nApply the same TTL validation from `alterCollectionTask.PreExecute` (added in #46717) to the REST API v2 `collections/create` handler, before the request is forwarded to the gRPC layer.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/milvus-io/milvus/issues/comments/4574915821/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/milvus-io/milvus/issues/comments/4826497720","html_url":"https://github.com/milvus-io/milvus/issues/49843#issuecomment-4826497720","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/milvus-io/milvus/issues/49843","id":4826497720,"node_id":"IC_kwDODHDyxM8AAAABH66CuA","user":{"login":"stale[bot]","id":26384082,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90MjYzODQwODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1724